      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "HOW MANY PLAYERS"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Cap Blanc": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Whitecape"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Cartes de territoire": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Territory cards"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Ce n'est pas la carte que vous aviez tirée : le camp qu'on vous demandait d'abattre est tombé sous d'autres coups. Elle s'est retournée en ce repli, pour que vous puissiez encore gagner.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "This is not the card you drew: the side you were asked to bring down fell to somebody else's blows. It turned over into this fallback, so you can still win."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Ce que chacun a montré savoir": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "What each player has shown they know"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Ce que chacun cherchait": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "What each player was after"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Celui qui ouvre la partie choisit pour tout le monde.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Whoever opens the game chooses for everyone."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Celui qui ouvre la table choisit pour tout le monde.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Whoever opens the table chooses for everyone."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Celui qui ouvre part avec %lld hommes de moins : ici, la défense l'emporte, et ouvrir se paie.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Whoever opens starts %lld troops down: here the defense wins, and opening costs."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Ces deux-là ne vont pas ensemble : allumer l'une éteint l'autre. Prendre le monde entier, ou remplir sa conquête — il faut choisir la fin de la partie.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "These two do not go together: turning one on turns the other off. Take the whole world, or fill your conquest — you have to choose how the game ends."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Cet instant ne se relit plus": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "This moment can no longer be replayed"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Chacun chez soi, sur son propre réseau. Un code à six lettres suffit — ni compte, ni inscription.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Each at home, on their own network. A six-letter code is enough — no account, no sign-up."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Chacun reçoit au départ un objectif secret — deux continents, tant de places tenues, un camp à faire tomber — et le remplir gagne la partie. Le seuil de territoires se retire : la carte décide, ou personne. Le compte de la barre du haut ne dit alors plus rien de qui va gagner.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Everyone is dealt a secret objective at the start — two continents, so many places held, a side to bring down — and filling it wins the game. The territory threshold withdraws: the card decides, or nobody. The count in the top bar then says nothing at all about who is going to win."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Chacun son tour : l'appareil se passe avant chaque question.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Taking turns: the device is passed before each question."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Chapitre suivant": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Next chapter"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Chaque tour joué dépose un instant ici, tout seul.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Every turn played drops a moment here, on its own."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Chercher des joueurs": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Find players"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Chine": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "China"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Choisir un instant reprend la partie à partir de là, sans effacer celle-ci : la suite que vous jouerez sera rangée à part.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Choosing a moment resumes the game from there without erasing this one: what you play next is shelved separately."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Cinq cartes en main : l'échange est obligatoire.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Five cards in hand: the trade is compulsory."
          }
